# Structural path protection for the R1 release gate (round 1 review P2-2).
#
# `release/release-manifest.json` is the reviewed version-traceability
# baseline: regeneration → review diff → commit IS the release-approval
# acknowledgment (docs/RELEASE_GATE.md §2). This file names the maintainer
# as the code owner of that baseline so the "re-approval" requirement can
# become STRUCTURAL, not merely procedural.
#
# NOTE: a CODEOWNERS file alone does not enforce review. It takes effect
# when branch protection enables "Require review from Code Owners" — a
# repository-settings action that cannot be set from a PR (documented as a
# follow-up in the PR description and docs/RELEASE_GATE.md §2).
# GitHub discovers this file at the repository root, .github/ or docs/;
# .github/CODEOWNERS is the conventional location.
/release/release-manifest.json @lybym
